      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A few things worth mentioning:\n\nLaunch options are not unique to steam. There are many ways to launch VRChat with as many launch options as you want, such as using VRC quick launcher, creating a shortcut, or using cmd.\n\nAnd even if that was a limitation:\n\n--watch-worlds is not something you want unless you're doing a local test.\n\n--enable-sdk-log-levels is mostly irrelevant now with udon debug logging.\n\n--fps=120 is no longer needed now that you can set framerate cap in the settings menu.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-18T04:01:04.209Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Steam has 260 characters limit on Launch Option. Now VRChat have a bunch of arguments to modify the behaviour, they can be exceed the limit. So, I think some (or all) options should be written in configuration file.\n\nWriting down all options, it may be...\n\n--profile=0 --no-vr --affinity=00FFF --osc=9000:127.0.0.1:9001 --midi=deviceName --enable-debug-gui --enable-sdk-log-levels --enable-udon-debug-logging --watch-worlds --watch-avatars --disable-hw-video-decoding --fps=120\n\nOptions above are 220 characters in total...",
